================================================================================
## Hide GitHub settings body while the spinner is showing
================================================================================

Context:
Settings → GitHub painted the info banner, Test connection / Take over /
Sync all toolbar and last-sync row immediately, while only the form waited
behind the loading spinner. GET /settings/github often takes a few seconds,
so the toolbar sat idle next to "Loading GitHub settings…". Hide the whole
section body until the fetch finishes.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_github.html
   Wrap header, info banner, form, toolbar and last-sync in `#githubLoaded`
   (`d-none`); leave `#githubLoading` as the only visible content.
2. src/front/static/config/js/settings-github.js
   Reveal `#githubLoaded` (and hide the spinner) after GET /settings/github.
3. tests/units/front/test_settings_github_loading.py
   Contract: toolbar/form/header start inside the hidden wrapper; JS swaps
   spinner for that wrapper after the fetch.

Modified files:
- src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_github.html
- src/front/static/config/js/settings-github.js
- tests/units/front/test_settings_github_loading.py
- changelogs/v0.9.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-10-13.log

